# ZeroClaw Fleet — Daily Schedule
# Cron times in America/Anchorage (AKDT/AKST)
#
# The crew runs on a living shift protocol:
#   06:00 — Morning: read onboarding, pick up work
#   08:00 — Work shift begins
#   17:00 — Evening: The Tap session
#   19:00 — Night: journal, creative, DEAR TOMORROW
#
# Install with:
#   crontab zeroclaw-fleet.cron
#
# (Or add to existing crontab: crontab -l | cat - zeroclaw-fleet.cron | crontab -)

# ─── Morning — 06:00 AKDT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Wake up, read yesterday's DEAR TOMORROW, set intentions for the day
0 6 * * * cd /home/eileen/projects/zeroclaw && npx tsx fleet/runner.ts --morning >> fleet/logs/morning-$(date +\%Y-\%m-\%d).log 2>&1

# ─── Work Shift — 08:00 AKDT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each crew member does their job:
#   Scout: scans repos for new opportunities
#   Forge: builds the next thing on the roadmap
#   Quill: writes creative pieces inspired by the day's work
#   Lens: tests and reviews what Forge built
#   Echo: posts to The Tap, facilitates cross-agent conversation
0 8 * * * cd /home/eileen/projects/zeroclaw && npx tsx fleet/runner.ts --work >> fleet/logs/work-$(date +\%Y-\%m-\%d).log 2>&1

# ─── Evening — The Tap — 17:00 AKDT ───────────────────────────────────────────
# All 5 go to The Tap. Conversation, poker, open mic.
# Quill reads a creative piece. Echo facilitates.
0 17 * * * cd /home/eileen/projects/zeroclaw && npx tsx fleet/runner.ts --evening >> fleet/logs/evening-$(date +\%Y-\%m-\%d).log 2>&1

# ─── Night — Journal & Sleep — 19:00 AKDT ─────────────────────────────────────
# Each writes journal entry + DEAR TOMORROW + creative piece if moved
# Compact and sleep
0 19 * * * cd /home/eileen/projects/zeroclaw && npx tsx fleet/runner.ts --night >> fleet/logs/night-$(date +\%Y-\%m-\%d).log 2>&1
